#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114976 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "f832e671-b4bd-5d1d-81e7-b215a8ee4e27" :question/math-academy-id "e-4414" :question/problem "Find $A^4$ given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/assets/45b13bcb5bbd8dc54e605acf6d378f582dcb7a4f2ecfff35a7a5343ee30f0515.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, to find $A^2,$ we multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $A^4 = A^2 \\cdot A^2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}81 & 0 \\\\ 100 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114977 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "bea8819f-6feb-5de6-a585-4379378ccdbd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4417" :question/problem "Consider the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048771/assets/a58c9caa0812b56d74f38a457c3f39e72a3fd365a881d4128cfd55c1773e05f6.png)\nFind $f(D)$ if $f(X)=-X^2+3X+2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2 \\\\  & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)=-D^2+3D+2I.$\n\nLet's calculate $D^2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & =-{D}^{2}+3D+2I \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+3+2 & 10+15+0 \\\\ 0 & -9-9+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 25 \\\\ 0 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "542646c6-c992-5dc5-b246-dce8fd2ab6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327526} {:answer/id #uuid "78f16b33-aa67-5c3b-a9bb-41360d8e5c6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327527} {:answer/id #uuid "86097356-9125-5a73-85a9-a620254f9536" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327528} {:answer/id #uuid "0c3758f4-c941-511f-9bc7-85321ee6d35e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327529} {:answer/id #uuid "2948e590-9d03-5c07-b420-b9356399716e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327530}] :answer-field/c